11	 * list column (no status line), one central surface that is either the list or the
12	 * reader (never both), and contact context. Account/Activity/Drafts live in
13	 * explicit labelled utility disclosures instead of permanent competing columns;
14	 * the contact pane shows only exact known fields.
15	 *
16	 * Keyboard contract (window-level, one handler):
17	 * - j / ArrowDown, k / ArrowUp: move conversation focus in the list (row focus
18	 *   follows). Inside the reader only j/k switch conversations; ArrowUp/Down
19	 *   keep native scrolling there.
20	 * - Enter: open the focused conversation. Escape: close the active utility or
21	 *   contact disclosure first, then the reader.
22	 * - e: archive the focused (or reader-open) conversation when actions are enabled.
23	 * - Shift+E: restore to Inbox; G then E (within 1000ms): cached Done.
24	 * - Left from list navigation: destination navigator; pointer Commands opens palette.
25	 * - Cmd+K opens the palette in native mode only (browser reservations stay native).
26	 * - c: compose a new local draft in the inline compose card in the central pane (works from list and reader).
