DESIGN.md:194:- **Reader:** the pane has no side padding. The reader's scroller carries the content inset (`padding-inline: 50px 24px`), so the subject, meta row, notes, loading identity and skeleton start at 50px, the same x as the list's sender text. The message stack keeps the list's focus-fill idea: each `.message` fill (the active one is Lifted Charcoal plus a 3px Dusk Lavender inset bar) spans from 6px to 6px of the pane edges, while its text stays on the inset (negative inline margin on `.messages`, inline padding on `.message`). Right edge decision: the right inset is 24px, the same as the dock, notices and composer, and the line measure is capped by `max-width: 65ch` on prose and `88ch` on monospace bodies, not by the container, so a wide pane stays left-aligned on the grid. The active message's toggle has two cues that mean different things: the 3px lavender bar says "this is the active message", and a 2px Paper White ring at a 1px offset, only on `:focus-visible`, says "the keyboard is here" (every other control keeps the lavender ring; the One Signal Rule holds because lavender still appears once). Measured at 1280×800: toggle outline `solid 2px rgb(255,255,255)` offset 1px, ring left edge at x=87 inside the message fill (46). The collapsed sender, the expanded body, the signature, `Details` and the `Show quoted text` label share one x (the message toggle and the `Details` summary carry no inline padding; the quote button pulls its 8px ghost padding into the gap with a `-8px` margin, like the selection actions: on a replica with the real class the label is at x=90 like the body, the button box at 82; before, the label was at 98). The selection-scope note and the in-pane recovery banner use the same 50px/24px. A docked composer (the reply composer and the docked new-message card) uses the undocked card's margins: `6px 24px 12px 50px`. The loading skeleton rows have the real collapsed-message pitch (1px border, 1rem padding, `--message-row-height` of 2 × Body, 0.5rem margin; about 49px at a 16px root) and start where the first message will, so the pane does not jump when the conversation arrives: the sender, date and `Loading conversation…` are ONE line (`role="status"` on the status span only); where the loaded reader has a meta row (read controls, read-only, a selection scope) that line IS the meta row's slot, and otherwise it is drawn out of flow over the first placeholder row (`.is-overlay`), which therefore paints no bar of its own. Without a list-row identity the subject slot is a hidden `h2.reader-subject` with a bar inside, so its margins match the real subject by construction. Measured in a browser with a deliberately delayed `getConversation` (fixture, no read controls, 1280×800): before, the first skeleton row was at y=244.3 and the first real message at y=187.9 (+56.4px); after, rows [187.9, 236.9, 285.9] against messages [187.9, 236.9, 285.9] (0.0px), also 0.0px at 1000×700 with a 20px root font (rows 213.2/274.2/335.2) and, as a replica with the meta-row classes and a real-shaped `.reader-meta-row`, 204.1 against 204.1. The rest of these numbers come from the CSS and are asserted by `tests/reader/geometry.test.ts`.
DESIGN.md:207:2. **Rail.** Done (2026-11-07 rail/contact layout pass). The rail is a fixed 40px column (px, so larger root fonts widen the list, never the rail) with a 1px Seam on its right.
DESIGN.md:234:12. **Command overlay.** Done (polish pass; structure pass: groups, per-command glyphs, aliases, Keys list, "no match" copy, caption removed). The off-palette values the overlay still carried (#56534e border and rules, #c9c4bc caption, icon and hint text, #d4cfc7 disabled reasons, #66615b `kbd` fill, `.85rem` radius, the 46rem width, 24px query and 1.5rem glyph) are now tokens: a 576px Lifted Charcoal panel with a 10px radius, no border, Overlay lift over a `rgba(0,0,0,0.53)` backdrop at 15vh. The query is 16px on Deep Umber with a 1px Dusk Lavender border, items are 36px rows of 12px Body with 16px Graphite glyphs, the highlighted item is Focus Stone plus a 3px Dusk Lavender bar, disabled items are Smoke with Ash reasons, and `kbd` is Ash on Deep Umber. Geometry is whole-pixel so a highlighted item scrolled into view is never clipped. The modal attachment chooser shares the panel (46rem wide, 12px body), which closes the "chooser body inherits 16px" remainder of gap 14. (The violets this gap once listed were already gone before this pass.)
DESIGN.md:236:14. **Type scale and dates.** Done (2026-11-07 typeset pass). The shell type is semantic tokens on `:root`: `--type-headline` 1rem, `--type-body` 0.75rem, `--type-count` 0.6875rem, `--type-mono` 0.85rem, weights 400/600 only (`--weight-regular`, `--weight-strong`). `.app-main` sets Body as the shell default, so the rail, contact pane, notices, drawers, the reader chrome and form controls are 12px instead of an inherited 16px or ad hoc 0.8/0.85/0.9/0.95/1.1rem. Shell h2 is Headline; h3/h4 and in-panel drawer headings are Title; the reader subject is Headline at 600. Row dates follow the Label rules below and are deterministic (no default-locale dependence: the old `30 Sept 2001` vs `Sep 30, 2001` rendered-layout gate now passes under any `LANG`). Rows carry `<time datetime>` plus the full date as the title; reader message times are full dates with `datetime`. The rendered larger-text gate expected the compact action disclosure at a 25px root font (was 23px) after this pass, and at 34.5px (expanded at 30px) after the rail/contact pass, since the fixed-px rail and contact pane leave the list wider at every text size.
DESIGN.md:241:   - **Compact docked reply composer.** A one-line recipient row (`To  Ada Fixture`) replaces the always-open To, Cc and Subject boxes. The row is a real button; while To still equals the default sender mailbox it shows the display name and the real address beside it (`Ada Fixture <ada@example.test>`, the address in Ash, never hover-only, so a sender named "Bank Support" cannot hide `x@evil.test`; a name equal to the address is not repeated), and the raw To text in an input as soon as it differs, so the field is never misrepresented. A quiet Ash `Cc / Subject` toggle (`aria-expanded`) opens those rows on demand; they open by themselves when Cc has text or the subject is not the default `Re:` line, so saved data is never hidden. An edited To does not open them: the To row is already a visible input then, so nothing is hidden. The heading follows the actual To, not the latest sender: while To is empty during creation, or equals the sender mailbox (case-insensitive), it reads `Reply draft to Ada Fixture`; otherwise it names the first entry of To (split on `,` or `;`) with ` +N` for N more (`Reply draft to list@lists.example +2`), and the full To is its title; a ready draft with an empty To reads `Reply draft`. This matters when the draft's To came from Reply-To on list or newsletter mail, where the sender and the recipient differ. The heading stays one short line for any number of addresses. The body is the dominant field and takes focus once the draft exists: at least six lines (7.5rem at the 12px body size), growing with its text up to half the viewport. The docked shell (`.reply-composer`, `.reader-pane > .compose-card`) is capped at 60% of the reader pane, so the thread stays above it, and it uses the same margins as the undocked card (`6px 24px 12px 50px`: left edge on the 50px inset, 24px at the right, 12px below), so docked and undocked composers agree. The read-only quoted block is Body type in the UI face, Ash, with the 2px Rule on its left edge, `pre-wrap`, clamped to three lines (the full snippet stays in the DOM); it is never part of the draft body. The new-message card keeps To and Subject as one-line label-plus-input rows with Cc on demand. The inputs are borderless-looking (a transparent 1px border with a Graphite underline at rest, the full Graphite border on hover, and Dusk Lavender with the inner ring on keyboard focus; see "Inputs / Fields"). The inline compose card, also where a reply draft is edited when its thread cannot host it, gap 21 shares the same core.
DESIGN.md:264:   - **24px content edge, rhythm, no borders.** Drawer content sits on the contact pane's inset (`--contact-inset`, 24px; the 50px list inset would leave a 460px drawer 360px) with 6px and 12px gaps and no off-scale rem gaps. `rule` is gone from drawer rows, the Activity group detail (no box; members indent 12px) and the Reminders fieldset.
DESIGN.md:314:   - **Header width rule (follow-up to the 1030px critique).** At the 1030px floor the preview tag, the account note, the read-only hint and the `Unread only` chip used to crush the active tab to 4px (measured x=90, w=4 on the old grid). Second pass: the header grid's tab column is `minmax(min(var(--header-tabs-floor), 100%), 1fr)` with a fixed `--header-tabs-floor: 10rem` (about `Inbox 18`, the 18px gap and the `Unread only` chip), so the tab strip never drops below it; the trail column takes what is left. Third pass (the 1030px critique with a saved split, `Unread only` and the read-only hint still left `Inbox` 13px wide with no label): the floor is built from what is really in the strip, `--header-tabs-floor: max(10rem, Inbox + saved tab + chips)` with `--tab-inbox: 4.5rem` (`Inbox 18` measured 62px), `--tab-saved: 9rem` (a saved label stops at `12ch` with an ellipsis, its full name is the tab's `title`, plus the count) and `--header-chip: 4.75rem` (`Unread only` measured 73px), plus the 18px gaps, added by `:has()` rules on the header for a second tab and for each chip. Tabs and the nav are `flex: 0 0 auto`: a tab never shrinks, so a note can never take a tab's label. At 1100px and below the read-only hint collapses to its `Review access` link (the words become visually hidden, so they stay in the accessibility tree and the hover title) and the link never clips, so the hint gives up width before anything else. Estimated at 1030px (list column 718px): tabs 328px, glyphs about 190px, collapsed hint about 90px; with the browser-preview Preview tag as well (never in the native app) the hint ellipsizes first. Inside the trail the glyphs are `flex: 0 0 auto` and never shrink; the notes shrink in this order: Preview tag (`flex-shrink: 4`, but never below 5.5rem), read-only hint (`2`), account status note (`1`, link fixed). Measured in a real browser at 1030px with the worst case (first sync failed, preview, chip): tabs 160px, `Inbox 18` 62px, chip 73px, preview 96px, status 244px, glyphs unmoved; the same content on the old grid gave tabs 4px. jsdom cannot lay anything out, so the tests pin the CSS rules (the floor variables and `:has()` rules, non-shrinking tabs, the `12ch` cap, the 1100px hint collapse) and the hint, ownership and action logic (`readOnlyHintShown`, `emptyLineOwnsStatus`, `headerNoteAnnounces`, `headerNoticeAction`), not the pixels. The third-pass floor was computed from the measured widths above and the tokens, not re-measured in a browser (none was available).
DESIGN.md:367:- **Headline** (400, 1rem / 16px, 1.25): split tabs and the contact name. This is the only large text in the shell.
DESIGN.md:368:- **Title** (600, 0.75rem / 12px, 1.35): sender names, contact email, section labels ("Mail"), footer labels, notice labels.
DESIGN.md:369:- **Body** (400, 0.75rem / 12px, 1.35): subject (Paper White), snippet and threads (Ash), date-group captions (Ash).
DESIGN.md:370:- **Label** (400, 0.75rem / 12px, tabular numerals): dates ("8:00 AM", "6 NOV" with an uppercase month) and counts in status text.
DESIGN.md:371:- **Reading** (400, 0.9375rem / 15px, 1.6): the message body, the signature and the quoted text in the reader, and nothing else. Tokens: `--type-reading` and `--leading-reading`. The measure is `65ch` for the proportional face. The 1.6 leading is the light-on-dark compensation: light text on Warm Charcoal needs more leading than the 1.35 of the 12px shell, and a measure this wide needs it too. The prose is Paper White; the signature and the quote are Ash. This is a deliberate third size outside the Two-Size Rule, which covers the browsing shell. **Mono fallback** (0.85rem, 1.45, `--type-mono`, `--leading-mono`; the Mono entry in the frontmatter): a body whose prose looks column-aligned (two consecutive lines indented by 4 spaces or a tab, or two or more lines with two or more pipes) keeps the monospace face at `88ch`, because hard-wrapped plain text is 72 to 78 columns. Quoted `>` lines do not trigger it. Neither measure has been checked against a render.
DESIGN.md:382:- **Count** (400, 0.6875rem / 11px): split-tab counts, set 4px after the tab label.
DESIGN.md:383:- **Mono** (400, 0.85rem, 1.45): the reader's plain-text body when its prose is column-aligned (the fallback described under Reading).
DESIGN.md:385:Sizes are rem so the 16px and 20px root-font layouts in `tests/browsing/inbox-list.rendered-layout.test.ts` still scale. Row and header heights are min-heights in px. The 12px row size is measured from the capture: system-ui glyph metrics point to 11.5–12px.
DESIGN.md:462:- **Shell:** Lifted Charcoal with a 1px Seam border, docked at the bottom of the reader pane (6px radius, capped at 60% of the pane) or, for a new message with no reader, the in-flow card (10px radius). Both use the margins `6px 24px 12px 50px`, so the card's left edge is on the 50px content inset in either place. Never a modal. A reply draft that cannot dock in its thread uses the same card, titled `Reply draft to …`, with one Amber Notice line under the heading (gap 21). Both share one inner padding, `--composer-padding` (`12px 16px 16px`); the reply composer used `0.4rem 0.6rem` (about 6/10px) before, and now measures `12px 16px 16px` like the card. The undocked new-message card is sized to its content (`flex: 0 1 auto`, still scrolling when the editor is taller than the column): 284.2px tall at 1280×800 (331px at a 20px root) instead of the 612.6px it filled with the footer at y=382 and about 345px of empty card below it.
DESIGN.md:464:- **Rows:** a 3.5rem Ash label column, then an input with a Graphite underline at rest (the full Graphite border on hover; Dusk Lavender plus the inner ring on keyboard focus); the reply shows only `To  <name> <address>` as a button until the user asks for more. Body: at least six lines, grows, with the same Graphite boundary as the rows.
DESIGN.md:469:- **Details:** a native `<details>`/`<summary>`, so the expanded state is exposed without ARIA. The `▸`/`▾` glyph is generated content in Ash with an empty alt (`content: '▸ ' / ''`, after the plain declaration as a fallback), so assistive technology reads `Details` only. Inside, From, To, `Cc` and Sent, in two columns: a fixed 3rem Ash label column, then the values, which therefore share one x (measured at 1280×800: 144.4px for all four, with `Details` at 90px; before, the labels sized to their text and the values started at 126.1, 109, 111.4 and 123.7; at a 20px root all four are at 158px and no label overflows). From and each To recipient are `role="group"` tab stops (they drive the contact pane; closed Details content is not focusable) with one accessible name, `Name, mailbox` or the bare mailbox, and the visible `Name <mailbox>` text is `aria-hidden` so the address is read once. Their keyboard focus is a 2px Dusk Lavender outline at a 1px offset, not a colour change alone. The cached message has no Cc, so the Cc row reads `Not cached` (Ash plain text, with a title that says Cc is not stored in the local cache and reply recipients are not inferred from it); Cc is never inferred or shown as empty.

